  "notes": [
    "Prices are the public API list prices. Usage on a subscription plan is shown as an 'API equivalent', not as money actually spent.",
    "Anthropic thinking tokens and OpenAI reasoning tokens are billed as output and are already included in output counts.",
    "cache_write_5m missing => cache writes billed as normal input; cache_write_1h missing => same as cache_write_5m.",
    "long_context applies per request when the full prompt size exceeds 'threshold' input tokens.",
    "speed_multipliers / geo_multipliers multiply every token category (not per-request fees).",
    "For Claude 4.x models the price page lists input/output; their cache prices here are derived from the documented standard multipliers (5m write 1.25x, 1h write 2x, read 0.1x).",
    "Gemini prices are the Gemini Developer API Standard tier. Gemini 3.6/3.7/3.8 Flash list an introductory price until 2026-12-31 (input 1.50, output 7.50, cache read 0.15 from 2027-01-01). Gemini caching has no write fee; thinking tokens are billed as output.",
    "Antigravity names some models by internal ids (gemini-3.8-flash-n, gemini-3-flash-a/-b/-c, -low/-medium/-high/-tiered thinking levels, claude-*-thinking and claude-*-low/-medium/-high, gpt-oss-*-maas); they are aliases of the model Antigravity shows for them. gemini-3-flash-a/-b/-c are served for Gemini 3.5 Flash at every thinking level. Antigravity does not report cache writes for Claude models, so those are counted as input."
  ],
